# The CLIENT example page IS committed. Only the internal build is ignored.
#
# Why the client example ships: `build-tracker.py` is the actual template — all
# the HTML, CSS and JS live inside it as Python strings — but nobody should have
# to run Python just to see what the thing looks like. Committing the rendered
# example makes the template reviewable on GitHub, in a fresh clone, or by
# someone evaluating it rather than building with it. It is fictional
# placeholder data, so there is nothing to leak.
#
# Why the INTERNAL build never ships: this template's one real promise is that
# internal content cannot reach a client-readable surface. The parent theme is
# deployed to every client site and its files are publicly fetchable, so a file
# literally named `*.internal.html` sitting at a public URL on every install
# contradicts that promise — even with fictional data — and bakes in a habit
# that will eventually be repeated with real data.
#
# A CHILD theme is the same shape: commit your `round-N.html`, because that file
# IS the deliverable; never commit `*.internal.html`. See README.md.
*.internal.html
